WEBVTT

00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:29.350
Goto-san!

00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:29.350
Detective Goto!

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:30.550
Are you all right?!

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:39.960
Yakumo, this circle of despair and sadness is far from over.

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:45.360
What I've been seeking...

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:49.750
is your hatred.

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:56.240
I've been awaiting this day!

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:10.760
Your body is now mine.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:29.410
Yakumo-kun...

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:40.950
Wh-What in the world's happening?

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:46.300
Ghosts are unable to completely control a human body

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:50.510
because when two souls try to coexist,

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.840
the body can't withstand the strain and will attempt to reject the foreign soul.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:59.220
Furthermore, I exploited this very fact to gain my freedom.

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:08.290
There's only one way of overcoming the body's inclination to reject the soul.

00:02:08.290 --> 00:02:15.200
If the mental states of the human and the ghost are virtually identical,

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:20.970
the two souls can be harmonized and the ghost can assume complete control over the body.

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:23.950
And that is our ultimate objective.

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:26.960
Harmonization.

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:33.900
Despair and enmity. The two violent emotions that shape <i>him</i>.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:39.720
And now that Yakumo's succumbed to enmity, <i>he</i> can finally harmonize with him.

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:42.030
Just a little longer.

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:46.610
Soon <i>he</i> will be reborn with a body.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:53.480
Yakumo's soul will be completely engulfed by <i>his</i> and disappear without a trace.

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:11.740
It looks like <i>he</i> is done.

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:16.480
Once I finish you all off, our plan will be complete.

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:20.640
Who shall I start with?

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.260
I guess it really has to be you after all...

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:27.620
Ozawa Haruka.

00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:36.570
Wait.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:49.580
It <i>is</i> you, right?

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:58.340
I was tired of waiting... for this day.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:04.330
To think I can touch you once more.

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:06.210
Hold me.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:09.730
Hold me tightly!

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:22.620
I finally understand why <i>he</i> attacked me so relentlessly.

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:25.620
Don't tell me you...

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:30.750
That's right. <i>He</i> does not exist within me.

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:43.890
Bitch!

00:04:56.180 --> 00:04:59.400
Don't worry. This is just a scratch.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:00.980
I'll call for a doctor.

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:02.530
Oh, thanks.

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:30.350
Yakumo-kun...

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:37.360
I'm sorry, I worried you.

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:47.620
Is that...

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:50.870
Yes, it's my uncle's contact lens.

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:58.130
Welcome home, Yakumo.

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:14.230
You... tricked me, eh?

00:06:14.230 --> 00:06:16.450
Ishii, shoot her.

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:18.230
B-But...

00:06:31.130 --> 00:06:33.290
Don't worry, Haruka.

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:38.250
I will protect you.

00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:08.270
Why?

00:07:08.270 --> 00:07:11.160
Why haven't you changed?

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:14.640
Where is <i>he</i>? What did you do to <i>him</i>?

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:26.550
You took a great risk to discover my true objective.

00:07:26.970 --> 00:07:29.790
I didn't harmonize with you.

00:07:29.790 --> 00:07:37.280
But you are still my son. We're bound by blood.

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:40.710
No, you're not my father.

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:43.470
My father is...

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:48.320
Saito Isshin.

00:08:00.010 --> 00:08:05.460
I really hate you for what you've done to my uncle.

00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:14.970
I even want you to suffer as I am by allowing your daughter to die.

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:19.740
However, if I do, you would hate me.

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:24.630
I don't want to be chained by the circle of hatred.

00:08:34.020 --> 00:08:37.120
I consent to the organ donation.

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:46.260
Just promise me one thing.

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:51.410
Once the transplant is completed, you will surrender yourself to the police and confess to your crimes.

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:57.890
You will... you will... save my daughter?

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:03.650
You're...

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:21.160
No matter what despair or hatred I experience, I'll never be dragged into the darkness.

00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:25.170
You can no longer defeat me.

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:32.550
Don't ever show yourself in front of us again.

00:09:39.310 --> 00:09:42.360
Yakumo, you should know...

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:49.700
As a ghost, there's no way you can capture me or make me disappear.

00:09:50.450 --> 00:09:54.570
A ghost is just a cluster of emotions.

00:09:54.570 --> 00:10:02.330
Until I fulfill my objective, I shall continue to exist in this form-for all eternity if necessary.

00:10:06.180 --> 00:10:09.590
Yakumo, we'll meet again.

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:18.880
Wait!

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:20.870
Don't leave me behind!

00:10:24.380 --> 00:10:29.080
You're also a victim. Your life was ruined.

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:31.360
I don't want to hear that.

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:36.360
However, the numerous crimes you've committed can't be forgiven.

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:37.160
Give <i>him</i> back!

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:38.640
Give <i>him</i> back to me!

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:40.410
You still don't understand?

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:44.030
<i>His</i> sole objective was me.

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:49.420
To <i>him</i>, you were nothing but a tool.

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:52.250
I knew that! Right from the very start!

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:55.300
<i>He</i> talked about you, day after day!

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:59.430
<i>He</i> didn't love me at all...

00:11:00.580 --> 00:11:07.020
But... I will still follow him.

00:11:07.690 --> 00:11:08.940
Wait!

00:11:12.780 --> 00:11:14.520
Please take care of Detective Goto.

00:11:28.210 --> 00:11:31.750
The fugitive Nanase Miyuki has been spotted in the vicinity of the Seta Mountains.

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:33.800
Take her in.

00:11:39.310 --> 00:11:43.870
Take a key and lock her up.

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:49.140
Lock her up. Lock her up.

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:54.530
Take a key and lock her up.

00:11:54.870 --> 00:11:59.530
My fair lady...

00:12:05.890 --> 00:12:07.790
I love you, Yakumo.

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:10.290
So much that I want to ruin you.

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:32.180
Goto-san's operation went well.

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:34.500
How is he?

00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:39.430
Knowing him, he'll probably be walking around in a few days.

00:12:39.950 --> 00:12:41.450
Thank goodness.

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:43.950
Are you okay, Yakumo-kun?

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:46.330
I'll be fine once I get some rest.

00:12:47.560 --> 00:12:49.620
I've signed the documents.

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:50.710
Documents?

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:53.640
The consent forms needed for the organ transplant to go ahead.

00:12:54.220 --> 00:12:56.840
That means Isshin-san will...

00:13:04.290 --> 00:13:08.130
This is my uncle's wish.

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:20.020
That bastard Sakakibara... Of course I can't forgive him.

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:25.190
But I think I can understand him... just a bit.

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:33.750
My dear...

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:34.750
What is it?

00:13:35.670 --> 00:13:38.250
There's something I want to discuss with you.

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:42.510
What a coincidence. Me too.

00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:55.100
Oh, Mom, is there anything I can help with?

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:56.820
I'm okay.

00:13:56.820 --> 00:13:59.270
You can keep Yakumo-kun company.

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:12.920
<i>He</i> was uneasy about his true self being discovered before <i>he</i> could fulfill his real objective,

00:14:12.920 --> 00:14:16.700
so <i>he</i> made it seem as if <i>he</i> attacked Isshin-san himself.

00:14:16.700 --> 00:14:22.510
Nanase Miyuki played the important role of informing the police by foretelling the murder.

00:14:22.510 --> 00:14:24.170
That wasn't all.

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:30.570
By ensuring she was arrested, she made us all believe <i>he</i> did it.

00:14:32.710 --> 00:14:34.560
That hurts, bastard!

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:40.440
Detective Goto, you sneaked out of the hospital?

00:14:40.800 --> 00:14:42.360
You're being too reckless.

00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:45.310
I know.

00:14:45.310 --> 00:14:48.570
And? How's the search at the lake going?

00:14:48.880 --> 00:14:51.060
Apparently they're ending it tomorrow.

00:14:51.060 --> 00:14:55.210
It seems like we won't be able to find the corpse.

00:14:55.210 --> 00:14:59.840
It's not possible that Nanase Miyuki is still alive, is it?

00:15:03.770 --> 00:15:06.880
What's so funny, you disgusting geezer?

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:12.060
I was just thinking that the living are full of sin.

00:15:12.610 --> 00:15:14.420
Just think about it.

00:15:14.420 --> 00:15:18.440
<i>He</i> never actually commits the crimes himself.

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:27.670
<i>He</i> just appears in front of those with weak souls or those that are enslaved by overwhelming greed

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:30.090
and deludes them into committing the crimes for him.

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:41.550
Perhaps <i>he</i> is a cluster of human sins.

00:15:42.440 --> 00:15:45.710
Human sins, eh?

00:15:55.170 --> 00:15:56.700
It's light.

00:15:56.700 --> 00:16:00.850
I hear he donated most of his organs.

00:16:02.800 --> 00:16:04.400
That's just like you, old man.

00:16:08.970 --> 00:16:12.260
I heard Yoshiko-chan had her operation yesterday.

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:14.540
Then she must've received Isshin-san's...

00:16:15.170 --> 00:16:19.500
There's no way we'll know for sure, but I certainly hope so.

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:26.820
Thank you very much.

00:16:30.750 --> 00:16:32.100
Are you satisfied?

00:16:32.100 --> 00:16:33.890
Now, get in.

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:36.890
You want to adopt Nao?

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:39.610
My wife and I talked about it.

00:16:39.610 --> 00:16:43.570
We decided we'd like to officially adopt Nao as our daughter.

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:48.780
But if you do that, I'll also become a part of your family.

00:16:48.780 --> 00:16:49.490
What?

00:16:51.630 --> 00:16:54.780
We're already in a family-like relationship to begin with.

00:16:55.100 --> 00:16:56.540
You're sending chills down my back.

00:16:56.820 --> 00:16:59.290
S-Same here.

00:16:59.850 --> 00:17:05.530
Besides, although your wife looks like she'll make a good mother, I doubt you'll make a good father.

00:17:05.530 --> 00:17:08.930
No one's a father from the very beginning.

00:17:08.930 --> 00:17:11.800
He only learns to be one after he starts raising a child.

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:15.050
That's unexpectedly wise coming from you.

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:18.810
If you're planning to be Nao's father, then...

00:17:23.650 --> 00:17:25.140
Fine!

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:33.570
Did Yakumo-kun pretend to be mad just so that he could trick his father and Nanase Miyuki?

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:42.290
Although I can't say for sure, I think he was truly sad and angry at the same time.

00:17:42.920 --> 00:17:46.090
Yet he wasn't consumed by <i>him</i>?

00:17:51.280 --> 00:17:57.220
Isshin-san said this to me shortly after I met Yakumo-kun:

00:17:57.690 --> 00:18:04.420
"I believe that one day his heart will be as clear as this sky."

00:18:48.030 --> 00:18:50.270
So, you're still here.

00:18:51.710 --> 00:18:54.040
You worry too much.

00:18:56.390 --> 00:19:00.890
There's no need for me to hide my red eye any more.

00:19:02.300 --> 00:19:06.110
Both Nao and I are fine now.

00:19:06.920 --> 00:19:11.300
And although we may not be related, we have a family.

00:19:15.680 --> 00:19:16.710
So...

00:19:17.980 --> 00:19:20.800
you should move on.

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:37.920
He really left.

00:19:38.370 --> 00:19:41.580
Did Isshin-san say anything?

00:19:42.510 --> 00:19:44.370
He said that he had a happy life.

00:19:45.220 --> 00:19:47.030
He had a huge smile on his face.

00:19:49.110 --> 00:19:50.210
And...

00:20:00.680 --> 00:20:03.100
"Thank you."

00:20:12.190 --> 00:20:15.610
You're not alone.

00:20:22.900 --> 00:20:25.390
Mom, do you have any lipstick with you?

00:20:25.390 --> 00:20:26.290
Why?

00:20:26.290 --> 00:20:27.870
Can I borrow it?

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:31.410
I'll clean it off immediately. It's just for a little while.

00:20:32.400 --> 00:20:33.880
I knew it. They look identical.

00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:36.630
Yoshiko, who does it resemble?

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:41.390
The man who taught me the value of life.

00:20:41.390 --> 00:20:43.390
Goto's left already?!

00:20:43.390 --> 00:20:47.600
He mentioned he had nothing further to do, so he just left.

00:20:48.330 --> 00:20:49.670
I guess I've got no choice.

00:20:49.670 --> 00:20:51.920
You'll suffice. Come with me.

00:20:51.920 --> 00:20:53.560
No, I...

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:55.290
Stop complaining!

00:20:56.340 --> 00:20:59.190
H-Help me, Makoto-san!

00:20:59.910 --> 00:21:02.910
It's late March and spring is in full bloom.

00:21:03.350 --> 00:21:06.980
It's the perfect season to dissect corpses.

00:21:09.290 --> 00:21:11.350
What would you like for dinner tonight?

00:21:11.970 --> 00:21:14.920
Hey, is there something you want to eat?

00:21:18.320 --> 00:21:21.330
She said anything that's tasty.

00:21:21.330 --> 00:21:24.640
That's no answer at all.

00:21:24.640 --> 00:21:25.720
Apparently.

00:21:28.780 --> 00:21:29.560
Hi.

00:21:31.980 --> 00:21:33.190
You again.

00:21:33.190 --> 00:21:35.110
You're sleeping again?

00:21:35.110 --> 00:21:37.490
"Spring is a sleepy season."

00:21:35.110 --> 00:21:37.490
Note: A verse from the poem "Spring Sleep" by Meng Haoran.

00:21:37.490 --> 00:21:39.960
I'm really sleepy during spring.

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:44.620
You mean you're sleepy all year-round.

00:21:44.620 --> 00:21:48.950
I don't want someone like you telling me that. In your head, it's always spring.

00:21:49.380 --> 00:21:52.080
Sure. Sure.

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:53.020
And?

00:21:53.020 --> 00:21:53.960
What?

00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:56.840
What kind of case did you bring me today?

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:06.470
Sensei, a new one's arrived.

00:22:06.470 --> 00:22:09.470
Oh, thank you for always bringing them.

00:22:09.470 --> 00:22:13.070
I see, so that's how it is.

00:22:15.520 --> 00:22:17.860
Thank you for your cooperation.

00:22:18.830 --> 00:22:20.240
It's no good.

00:22:20.240 --> 00:22:21.610
There's no end to this.

00:22:27.160 --> 00:22:29.370
Thank you, Chief.

00:22:34.260 --> 00:22:35.000
Here you go.

00:22:35.830 --> 00:22:37.450
It's delicious.

00:22:44.740 --> 00:22:46.040
Yakumo-kun.

00:22:46.530 --> 00:22:48.010
Thank you.
